Description: CVE-2026-64685 - Fix out-of-bounds read in BGR/BGRA/BGRO coder
 ReadBGRImage() read a scanline into the pixel stream once per output row
 but only validated the number of bytes actually read (count == length)
 once per row, before importing every channel plane. When a truncated file
 caused a short read, the per-channel import loop still processed all
 3 (BGR) or 4 (BGRA/BGRO) quantum planes from the undersized buffer,
 producing a heap out-of-bounds read (CWE-125).
 .
 The fix moves the pixel declarations and the length check inside the
 per-channel loop so the count == length validation is performed after each
 read, bailing out before any plane is imported from a short buffer.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/093f476e985d61557ea75ad0ef30d491dff816f3
