Description: CVE-2026-62343 - Fix heap buffer overflow when acquiring kernel values
 A heap-based buffer overflow (CWE-190 integer overflow leading to
 undersized allocation) occurs in MagickCore/morphology.c when acquiring
 the values array of a KernelInfo structure. The allocation size was
 computed as kernel->width * (kernel->height * sizeof(*kernel->values))
 without any overflow sanity checking, so a crafted kernel with large
 width/height dimensions could wrap the multiplication and cause a
 too-small buffer to be allocated, followed by out-of-bounds writes.
 .
 This patch introduces a helper AcquireKernelValues() that uses
 HeapOverflowSanityCheckGetSize() to validate the width*height product
 before allocating, and routes every kernel value allocation in
 ParseKernelArray(), AcquireKernelBuiltIn() and CloneKernelInfo() through
 it.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/9acf93f66b0f8495fa222e1a27c3db534cd78864
Author: ImageMagick <no-reply@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-31
